# Wiki Contract

The project keeps an Obsidian-style wiki at `wiki/` documenting product vision, domain, architecture, and phases.

**Before any docs ingest, query, lint, or update, read `wiki/index.md` and the relevant linked pages first. After any change, update every affected page, then refresh `wiki/index.md` and `wiki/log.md`.** Full schema: `wiki/AGENTS.md` and root `AGENTS.md`.

## When To Use It

- Onboarding or "how does this work / where is X" → `wiki/Getting Started.md`, then `index.md`
- Implementing a phase/feature → read `wiki/features/` + related concepts; update after the change
- Any new page/rename → update `index.md`, append to `log.md` (`## [YYYY-MM-DD] <ingest|query|lint|update> | <title>`)

## Canonical Pages By Topic

- Overview: `wiki/overview.md`
- Stack: `wiki/concepts/Tech Stack.md`
- Domain: `wiki/concepts/Domain Model.md`
- Inventory rules: `wiki/concepts/Document-Driven Inventory.md`
- Costing: `wiki/concepts/FIFO Costing.md`
- Accounting: `wiki/concepts/Inventory Accounting.md`
- Org structure: `wiki/concepts/Org Branch Location.md`
- POS boundary: `wiki/concepts/POS Integration Boundary.md`
- Phases: `wiki/features/Feature Phases.md`
- Spec ingest: `wiki/sources/`

## Page Conventions

- YAML frontmatter (`tags`, `created`, `updated`, plus `source_count` for entity/concept pages)
- Use `[[wikilinks]]` for internal links; end entity/concept pages with `## Sources`
- Use the `obsidian-markdown` skill when editing these files
